tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Whether or not we are in an electoral campaign, the party is always trying to broaden its voter base. Who should we focus our campaign efforts on?

- @workers: The urban working class, we could convince them to unionize.
- @new_middle: The "new middle class" of government employees and white-collar workers.
- @old_middle: The "old middle class" of small independent businessmen and artisans.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, who have felt neglected by us in the past.
- @unemployed: The unemployed, our traditional support base.
- @catholics: Catholics, who typically support the Center Party.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!
	 if (Q.kpd_formed == 0) {
		Q.workers_kpd += 6*(1-Q.dissent)
		Q.resources -= 1
		Q.grassroots_support += 4

		if (Q.unemployed >= 15) {Q.workers_kpd -= 2}
		if (Q.unemployed >= 25) {Q.workers_kpd -= 2}
		if (Q.wtb_adopted == 1) {Q.workers_kpd += 6*(1-Q.dissent)}
		if (Q.nationalization_progress >= 1) {Q.workers_kpd += 3*(1-Q.dissent)}
	}
	if (Q.kpd_formed == 1) { 
		Q.workers_kpd += 8*(1-Q.dissent)
		Q.resources -= 1
		Q.grassroots_support += 4

		if (Q.unemployed >= 15) {Q.workers_kpd -= 2}
		if (Q.unemployed >= 25) {Q.workers_kpd -= 2}
		if (Q.wtb_adopted == 1) {Q.workers_kpd += 6*(1-Q.dissent)}
		if (Q.nationalization_progress >= 1) {Q.workers_spd += 3*(1-Q.dissent)}
	}
!}

We have increased our campaigning among the workers. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?][? if nationalization_progress >= 1 : Nationalizing the economy gives us a new rallying point around which to attract workers. ?]

